      "notes": "Google published both advisories on its own repository on Sep 4 and Sep 6, 2026; NVD and the GitHub Advisory Database assigned and published the CVE IDs on Oct 19, so scanner visibility lags vendor fixes by six weeks - deployments that scanned clean last week now report findings. Google's advisory states the official deployment configuration shipped the wildcard policy, so default installs were exploitable, and the shipped 0.0.0.0 libp2p bind with DHT discovery left nodes reachable. Fixed in v0.1.0-alpha.9 (enrollment chain) and v0.1.0-alpha.3 (ingress bypass); current release v0.1.1. Reported by Eli Ainhorn (Noma Security) and Yanchon918s."
